{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Disposition change: this is NO LONGER deferred — it is being fixed together with parent 1137 in the same change (Gerrit #2399). Rationale: the plan-review gate on 1137 (LLM Pass, finding G6) flagged that fixing attest.py while leaving drift_floor.py:126's byte-identical unscoped head_sha read would leave two 'intentionally synchronized' stale-head anchors that could diverge. Rather than mirror the fix inline (re-introducing synchronized-by-copy fragility), we extracted a single shared helper gate_source.current_head_sha(auth_manifest, repo_root) that BOTH attest._unscoped_head_drift and drift_floor's code_drifted block now read, so they cannot diverge. drift_floor now catches SnapshotError -> 'unknown' (denies convergence, never suppresses findings — honoring drift_floor's own 'a broken signal can only DENY convergence, never suppress incorrectly' contract). Teeth tests added in tests/unit/test_plan_review_drift_floor.py (candidate reads the shared gate-ref anchor not the working tree; denies convergence when gate ref unresolvable). Will close this ticket once #2399 merges (Verified +1)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788051242475557001,"uuid":"ca35701d-7082-445c-8adb-9fd8e3ad7f9c"}